00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:29.200
Battery energy storage systems face a qualification bottleneck when serving AI data centers because

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:34.560
power quality and response times must match the instantaneous load swings of training clusters.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:40.520
In Vidya's new program tests exactly those parameters and selected only three suppliers,

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:44.700
connectors, which narrows the field to vendors already operating at utility scale.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:51.140
Tesla's inclusion alongside LG and Hitachi shows its mega-packed lineage already meets

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:56.280
the electrical and software thresholds that most residential or smaller commercial systems

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.680
have never been asked to clear.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.260
The economics shift once qualification is achieved.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:07.940
A single qualified supplier can bid on multi-hundred megawatt-hour projects that carry higher margins

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:14.220
than vehicle batteries, because the buyer values uptime over lowest sell cost. Tesla therefore

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:18.780
gains a second revenue stream that does not compete directly with its own vehicle production

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:25.180
for sell allocation. Yet the same qualification creates a moat for incumbents. New entrance

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:30.720
must now clear both technical and contractual hurdles before they can even quote on the next

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:36.700
wave of AI-driven storage demand, which concentrates capacity among the three named companies until

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:38.600
others catch up on testing cycles.

